  "behavior": [
    "UpdateObservations accepts explicit provider reset scopes. Each scope requires a successful complete replacement. Failed or canceled preparation preserves accepted state.",
    "Reset scopes, replacement observations, and accepted generation identity share the publication journal. Replay masks prior provider records without rewriting original receipts.",
    "The selected baseline, unrelated providers and bindings, and reviewed operator edits remain. Existing scheduled files are anchored before the first reset.",
    "Reset history changes generation identity even when the effective catalog payload is unchanged. Recovery resolves lost replies against that identity.",
    "Manual head and batch version 2 retain resets. The reader accepts legacy version 1 without resets and refuses unsupported or inconsistent records.",
    "Bounds cover 4096 batches and 64 MiB of encoded observations and reset scopes. Compaction remains CSP5 work."
  ],
